        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "37c26c2b-5bee-383f-a50d-d54f114dfa60",
                "word": "élatif",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "895aa562-72f4-4199-a092-e59dbe8b0a1e",
                        "entry_id": "37c26c2b-5bee-383f-a50d-d54f114dfa60",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "élatifs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b07b6564-ae3e-3d47-8c7e-c47a10e6ae6f",
                        "entry_id": "37c26c2b-5bee-383f-a50d-d54f114dfa60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Cas pouvant exprimer dans certaines langues (finnois, hongrois, estonien) le lieu de l’intérieur duquel provient un mouvement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbdca590-1c9a-4ebb-a1da-9c188a97d85c",
                                "sense_id": "b07b6564-ae3e-3d47-8c7e-c47a10e6ae6f",
                                "text": "En grammaire hongroise, l’élatif est marqué par un suffixe."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1407dd94-e3e1-3f4e-a017-1b693955f6e6",
                        "entry_id": "37c26c2b-5bee-383f-a50d-d54f114dfa60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Correspond à un des degrés de l’adjectif, à savoir, une forme de superlatif absolu dans certaines langues (arabe)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88da63fb-40d5-4ff5-bc5a-4570c3cf6d2c",
                                "sense_id": "1407dd94-e3e1-3f4e-a017-1b693955f6e6",
                                "text": "En arabe, l’élatif de كَبِير kabīr (« gros, grand ») est أَكْبَر ʾakbar (« plus gros, plus grand »)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8703650d-cd97-4233-8f0d-fb66087b1998",
                        "source_entry_id": "37c26c2b-5bee-383f-a50d-d54f114dfa60",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b6564-ae3e-3d47-8c7e-c47a10e6ae6f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Cas grammatical",
                        "target_lang_word": "Elativ",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Elativ",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a8227c4-64ac-3b9f-b90f-3740f2df5286",
                                        "entry_id": "e6a6a953-0b99-35a3-a85e-5898921752ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "absolut höchste Stufe der Steigerung der Adjektive; der Elativ wird im Deutschen durch den absoluten Superlativ oder besonders durch Adverbien ausgedrückt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd6e0ab4-7d72-4d4b-9574-268d18138d0b",
                                                "sense_id": "6a8227c4-64ac-3b9f-b90f-3740f2df5286",
                                                "text": "In „Hans ist ein äußerst großer Junge“ drückt das adverbiell verwendete Adjektiv äußerst den Elativ aus. Statt „äußerst“ kommen für den Elativ auch weitere Wörter wie „extrem“, \"sehr\", „unübertrefflich“ in Frage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "630a0a3f-1584-41c1-8eed-1831ef9fd8b5",
                                                "sense_id": "6a8227c4-64ac-3b9f-b90f-3740f2df5286",
                                                "text": "„Der Elativ ist also nicht eine eigene Komparationsform des Adjektivs, sondern eine besondere Gebrauchsweise des Superlativs.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25a074df-7b1e-4b52-bd60-135acbaa70dc",
                                                "sense_id": "6a8227c4-64ac-3b9f-b90f-3740f2df5286",
                                                "text": "„Bei den Adjektiven sind die verschiedenen Steigerungsformen zu beachten: der Positiv (die Normalform), der Komparativ (die Steigerungsform) und der Superlativ (die Höchststufe, die außerhalb von Vergleichen Elativ genannt wird).“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbcf6b68-e32d-43d9-b4d0-e6a05f501f8d",
                                                "sense_id": "6a8227c4-64ac-3b9f-b90f-3740f2df5286",
                                                "text": "„Das letztere ist der sogenannte Elativ.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03453dae-215b-34af-9ba9-2dd1f56daf0f",
                                        "entry_id": "e6a6a953-0b99-35a3-a85e-5898921752ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "unter anderem in den finnisch-ugrischen Sprachen ein Kasus der Richtung von innen nach außen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5649126f-a29f-469e-b701-6b4cf1920052",
                        "source_entry_id": "37c26c2b-5bee-383f-a50d-d54f114dfa60",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b6564-ae3e-3d47-8c7e-c47a10e6ae6f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Cas grammatical",
                        "target_lang_word": "elative",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "elative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e37fd6c-5726-3734-93b4-ffc42d304243",
                                        "entry_id": "da7d90f9-5386-31e4-ad01-4324ceadefd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Exalted; feeling elation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "300a312a-072c-4fef-b683-e24ebb30dd96",
                                                "sense_id": "9e37fd6c-5726-3734-93b4-ffc42d304243",
                                                "text": "And so the fleas, and flies in their degree, / By their attracted moyst humiditie, / Drawne from a certaine vertue elatiue, / Whence raine his generation doth deriue: / Seeke more than their accustom'd nutriment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14032dc3-cd96-4503-888b-8b7bddf4601b",
                                                "sense_id": "9e37fd6c-5726-3734-93b4-ffc42d304243",
                                                "text": "Thither shall gratitude's feelings elative wend, / Bath'd in the dew of the soul's lofty swelling."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfac3917-877d-44bc-93e3-425c1756b132",
                                                "sense_id": "9e37fd6c-5726-3734-93b4-ffc42d304243",
                                                "text": "The first case is that of E. M., 37 years of age, laborer, who on admission was elative, over-talkative, had a well marked feeling of well being."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6473cd7b-fc47-4b0e-a2d1-9dba49886dfd",
                                                "sense_id": "9e37fd6c-5726-3734-93b4-ffc42d304243",
                                                "text": "whereas if one thinks instead that it is inflicted by others, then the elative feeling is one of masochism, which is quite rightly deemed a disease."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "elative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "524ad0fd-12dd-31df-a2b3-fad86977cdf2",
                                        "entry_id": "bd7301e1-fffd-3257-969c-9e3ea04441e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In Semitic languages, the “adjective degree of superiority”. In some languages such as Arabic, the concepts of comparative and superlative degree of an adjective are merged into a single form, the elative. How this form is understood or translated depends upon context and definiteness. In the absence of comparison, the elative conveys the notion of “greatest”, “supreme.”"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "857b6a75-eaca-445c-abca-09436b46f033",
                                                "sense_id": "524ad0fd-12dd-31df-a2b3-fad86977cdf2",
                                                "text": "The elative of كَبِير (kabīr, “big”) is أَكْبَر (ʔakbar, “bigger/biggest, greater/greatest”)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "elative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0dcad79a-ba6e-3c5f-96a8-cf084114b77b",
                                        "entry_id": "8d5c6f6a-611d-3e3c-9096-e95b381a4412",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In Finno-Ugric languages, one of the locative cases, expressing “out of,” or “from” as in Finnish talosta, Hungarian házból (“out of the house”). Its opposite is the illative case (“into”). In Finnish, the case form is used also to express \\\"out of\\\" or \\\"proximity\\\" in a figurative sense which in English is often conveyed by the word \\\"about\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f160ea5a-b64a-4a69-a493-67d32668a7f9",
                        "source_entry_id": "37c26c2b-5bee-383f-a50d-d54f114dfa60",
                        "source_sense_id": "b07b6564-ae3e-3d47-8c7e-c47a10e6ae6f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Cas grammatical",
                        "target_lang_word": "elative case",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "elative case",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24f43de2-00e9-39d7-aa28-31e19272f34c",
                                        "entry_id": "1613ec73-2b91-31c9-b7c5-433aa3d7d0d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The case used to indicate movement out of something; for example, out of the house. Some languages that make use of the elative are Finnish, Hungarian, and Estonian."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
